From: Qore Technologies, s.r.o.
Subject: Enable C++ before configuring compiler warning flags for tests

EnableWarnings.cmake exports empty CXX flag variables when C++ is not yet
enabled. Those shadow CMake's later CXX cache initialization, losing Fedora's
hardening flags. The C++ ABI probe then links non-PIE objects with PIE linker
flags and cannot discover the compiler's implicit include directories.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -13,6 +13,10 @@
 INCLUDE (CheckLibraryExists)
 
 PROJECT (c-ares LANGUAGES C VERSION "1.34.8" )
+# Test targets use C++; initialize its flags before EnableWarnings.cmake.
+IF (CARES_BUILD_TESTS)
+  ENABLE_LANGUAGE(CXX)
+ENDIF ()
 
 # Set this version before release
 SET (CARES_VERSION "${PROJECT_VERSION}")
